WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.449 --> 00:00:05.160
Washing your hands with soap is possibly the
simplest way to flush pathogens down the drain.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:09.929
Soap molecules can interact with pathogens,
such as coronavirus leading to their destruction.

00:00:09.929 --> 00:00:12.290
Each molecule has 2 parts.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:16.940
The head is hydrophilic, which means it likes
to interact with water, while the lipid tail

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:22.680
is hydrophobic, which means it wants to get
away from water to find similar, water-avoiding particles.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.240
This is the basis of how soap works.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:33.100
When the molecules encounter lipid particles
on our skin, the tails aggregate around them

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.310
to form spherical structures called micelles, creating water-free environment.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.840
Similar thing happens when they encounter
enveloped viruses such as coronavirus.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.420
Enveloped viruses carry their genome and supporting
proteins inside a lipid bilayer membrane

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.680
with the proteins necessary for infection embedded
in the membrane.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.800
In cells and viruses these lipids are packed neatly into 2 sheets

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:04.160
with the lipid tails facing inward.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.680
The lipid ends of the soap molecules are attracted
to the lipids in the membrane.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:19.280
They take advantage of the presence of membrane
proteins, which can perturb the neatly organized

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.260
bilayer to insert themselves into the viral
membrane.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:28.880
If there is only a small amount of soap, the
soap molecules only loosen the membrane,

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:34.140
but with more soap, they begin to create micelles around membrane lipids.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.680
They are also attracted to hydrophobic amino
acids in the membrane proteins,

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:46.380
extracting them from the membrane.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:50.680
The structural integrity of a virus is essential
for infection.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:57.160
So, washing your hands with soap protects
you better from infection than washing with only water,

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:01.740
and the longer you lather, the
higher your chance of destroying the virus.

